<title>UK: Courtaulds indicated firmer on dividend.</title>
<headline>Courtaulds indicated firmer on dividend.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Courtaulds were indicated higher on Wednesday as traders focused on a higher dividend to be paid and shrugged off the weakness in interim profits.</p>
<p>The shares were up 7p to 431p at 0820 GMT in pre-market trading.  </p>
<p>Courtaulds said it would pay a dividend of 4.45p per share, which was on the high end of estimates, and posted interim pretax profits of 64.0 million stg, below analysts' forecasts of 65.0 million stg to 70.0 million stg.</p>
<p>-- Debra Sherman, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
